---
/**
 * Terms of service. Draft, unreviewed — see the notice at the foot.
 *
 * The limitation section matters more than usual here: a deadline tracker that
 * is mistaken for a guarantee of compliance is a liability, so the page says
 * outright what the product is not.
 */
import Public from '../layouts/Public.astro'
import { site } from '../lib/site.ts'

const updated = 'September 2026'
---

<Public title="Terms" description="The terms of using FleetView Compliance.">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Terms</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-500">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-ink-700">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 p-5">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-amber-900">
          What this service is not
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-amber-900">
          We are a record-keeping and reminder service. <strong>We are not a law firm, we do not
          give legal advice, and we do not file anything with any agency on your behalf.</strong>
          Using this service does not make you compliant, and nothing here is a guarantee that you
          are. Responsibility for meeting every obligation that applies to your business remains
          yours.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Accuracy</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-500">
          We take considerable care with the rules we encode and we cite them so you can check
          our work. Regulations change, agencies publish corrections, and public data sources are
          sometimes wrong or out of date. Where we are unsure, we tell you rather than guess.
          Verify anything that matters against the rule itself before you rely on it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Your account</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-500">
          You are responsible for what happens under your logins and for the accuracy of what you
          enter. Do not share credentials. Tell us promptly if you think an account has been
          compromised.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Your data</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-500">
          Your records remain yours. You may export them at any time. We use them to provide the
          service to you and for nothing else. See the <a href="/privacy" class="text-brand-600 hover:underline">privacy policy</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Payment</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-500">
          Billed monthly in advance at the published rate, based on the number of power units on
          your account. There is no contract and no minimum term — cancel whenever you like, and
          you will not be billed again. We do not refund part-months, but we will not bill you for
          a month you did not use.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Availability</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-500">
          We aim to keep the service running continuously but do not promise it will never be
          unavailable. Alerts depend on email and mobile networks we do not control. Do not treat
          an alert that did not arrive as evidence that a deadline did not exist.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-500">
          To the fullest extent the law allows, our total liability arising out of the service is
          limited to the amount you paid us in the twelve months before the claim. We are not
          liable for fines, penalties, lost business or consequential losses. Some of these
          limits may not apply to you where the law does not permit them.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Governing law</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-500">
          These terms are governed by the laws of the State of California.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-500">
          {site.email ? site.email : 'Contact details are on the About page.'}
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-10 rounded-lg bg-amber-50 px-4 py-3 text-sm text-amber-900">
      <strong>Draft.</strong> Not reviewed by a lawyer, and the operating entity is not yet named.
      Both must be done before launch.
    </p>
  </section>
</Public>
